# Every fault that must exist.
#
# Without this file, deleting a fault directory is a silent way to make the
# catalogue pass: fewer entries, all green, nothing to see. That is the same
# move as deleting a failing test, one level up, and it is cheaper because a
# fault has no obvious owner and its absence looks like it was never there.
#
# run-fault-catalogue.sh requires every name here to exist, and every
# directory present to be named here. Removing a fault stays allowed — a
# defect can genuinely stop being expressible — but it takes an edit to this
# file, which lands in the diff where a reviewer will see the entry and its
# why.md disappearing together.
#
# One name per line. Comments and blank lines ignored.

